# =============================================================================
# Zeek / Bro dns.log — Format Documentation
# =============================================================================
# Auto-detected by the presence of '#separator' and '#fields' directives
# AND 'uid' or 'id.orig_h' in the first 600 bytes.
# All lines beginning with '#' are part of the Zeek header or are comments.
#
# Standard field  ←  Zeek #fields column(s) used
# --------------  -----------------------------------------------------------
# timestamp       ← ts            (Unix epoch float → ISO-8601 UTC)
# domain          ← query         (trailing dot stripped)
# query_type      ← qtype_name    (preferred) or qtype (numeric, fallback)
# response_size   ← resp_ip_bytes (preferred) or orig_ip_bytes (fallback)
# query_length    ← computed from len(query) when absent
# subdomain_count ← computed from label count when absent
#
# Common Zeek dns.log #fields (not all are required):
#   ts uid id.orig_h id.orig_p id.resp_h id.resp_p proto trans_id rtt
#   query qclass qclass_name qtype qtype_name rcode rcode_name
#   AA TC RD RA Z answers TTLs rejected orig_ip_bytes resp_ip_bytes
# =============================================================================
#separator \x09
#set_separator	,
#empty_field	(empty)
#unset_field	-
#path	dns
#fields	ts	uid	id.orig_h	id.orig_p	id.resp_h	id.resp_p	proto	trans_id	rtt	query	qclass	qclass_name	qtype	qtype_name	rcode	rcode_name	AA	TC	RD	RA	Z	answers	TTLs	rejected
#types	time	string	addr	port	addr	port	enum	count	interval	string	count	string	count	string	count	string	bool	bool	bool	bool	count	vector[string]	vector[interval]	bool
